:1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:7e94322554f1fa892932fa346b4cca0928f9575a1a3fbc2307ae398b8550e9ac","file":"preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":33,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3b63e892f863d430a2521e06c6bcb8122721d5755257609e5d56253267b9b255","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7e94322554f1fa892932fa346b4cca0928f9575a1a3fbc2307ae398b8550e9ac","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Buffered-comparison-and-stopping-band-resolution-in-critical-Ising-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L33"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{in:comparison}\nFor every two configurations $b,b'$ on $J$ and every configuration $a$\non $I$,\n\\[\n e^{-4\\operatorname{arctanh}q_0}\n \\leq\n \\frac{\\mu(\\sigma_I=a\\mid\\sigma_J=b,\\sigma_F)}\n      {\\mu(\\sigma_I=a\\mid\\sigma_J=b',\\sigma_F)}\n \\leq e^{4\\operatorname{arctanh}q_0}.\n\\]\nEither conditional law may be replaced by an arbitrary mixture of\nthese laws. The bound is symmetric in the two terminal sets."}
